Figure 2 illustrates the in vivo distribution and clearance of Nano-11 nanoparticles after intramuscular injection. Whole-mouse imaging over 21 days reveals that the Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 remains largely localized at the injection site, with negligible distribution to internal organs by day 21. The fluorescent signal at the injection site shows an initial rapid decrease, a moderate increase on day 2, and then a steady decline, with approximately 20% of the original signal detectable by day 21, indicating gradual clearance of the nanoparticles from the injection site over time.